---
import SEO from "../components/SEO.astro";
---

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="Support Barkly Labs — an independent technology laboratory building human-centered systems, open technology, research infrastructure, and experimental tools."
  />
  <meta
    name="twitter:description"
    content="Help Barkly Labs build technology that adapts to humans."
  />
  <meta
    property="og:description"
    content="Support Barkly Labs and help build human-centered technology."
  />
  <meta
    property="og:title"
    content="Support the Lab — Barkly Labs"
  />
  <meta
    property="og:url"
    content="https://www.barklylabs.space/support/"
  />
  <link
    rel="canonical"
    href="https://www.barklylabs.space/support/"
  />
  <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Support the Lab — Barkly Labs</title>

  <SEO />
</head>

<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-logo">
      <a href={import.meta.env.BASE_URL + ""}>
        <span>BARKLY</span> <strong>LABS</strong>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="header-document">
      <span>SUPPORT</span>
      <span>/</span>
      <span>DOCUMENT 001</span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <aside class="side-nav">
      <a href="#mission">01 MISSION</a>
      <a href="#why">02 WHY SUPPORT</a>
      <a href="#funding">03 WHERE IT GOES</a>
      <a href="#ways">04 WAYS TO HELP</a>
      <a href="#sponsors">05 SPONSORSHIP</a>
      <a href="#transparency">06 TRANSPARENCY</a>
    </aside>

    <section class="hero-section" id="mission">
      <div class="section-number">01 / MISSION</div>

      <div class="hero-content">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          BARKLY LABS / SUPPORT THE LAB
        </div>

        <h1>
          HELP BUILD<br />
          <span>THE LAB.</span>
        </h1>

        <p class="hero-copy">
          Barkly Labs is building technology around a simple idea:
          <strong>people are worth designing for.</strong>
        </p>

        <p class="hero-copy muted">
          We build software, hardware, AI systems, documentation,
          research infrastructure, and experimental tools designed to
          make complex technology more understandable, accessible,
          creative, and human.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="primary-button" href="#ways">
            SUPPORT BARKLY →
          </a>

          <a class="secondary-button" href="/sponsors">
            SPONSOR THE LAB →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" id="why">
      <div class="section-number">02 / WHY SUPPORT</div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>
          THIS ISN'T<br />
          <span>JUST A WEBSITE.</span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="content-grid">
        <div class="content-block">
          <div class="block-label">01 / BUILD</div>
          <h3>WE BUILD REAL THINGS.</h3>
          <p>
            Barkly is an active laboratory. Projects become software,
            hardware, documentation, standards, experiments, and
            infrastructure that people can actually use.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
          <div class="block-label">02 / DOCUMENT</div>
          <h3>WE MAKE THE WORK UNDERSTANDABLE.</h3>
          <p>
            Good technology should not require everyone to already
            understand how it works. Barkly documents systems,
            decisions, requirements, interfaces, and experiments so
            other people can learn from them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
          <div class="block-label">03 / RELEASE</div>
          <h3>WE WANT KNOWLEDGE TO ESCAPE THE LAB.</h3>
          <p>
            Open projects are more useful when people can actually
            understand, reproduce, modify, and build on them.
            Barkly is designed around that idea.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="content-block">
          <div class="block-label">04 / HUMAN FIRST</div>
          <h3>PEOPLE COME BEFORE THE SYSTEM.</h3>
          <p>
            The Barkly Standard asks a different question:
            <strong>does this technology work for the human using it?</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="human-note">
        <span class="note-mark">♡</span>

        <div>
          <strong>
            TECHNOLOGY SHOULD ADAPT TO HUMANS.
          </strong>

          <p>
            That's the whole point.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section funding-section" id="funding">
      <div class="section-number">03 / WHERE IT GOES</div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>
          SUPPORT<br />
          <span>BECOMES INFRASTRUCTURE.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          Contributions help turn ideas into things that can actually
          be built, tested, documented, maintained, and shared.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="funding-grid">
        <article class="funding-card">
          <span class="funding-index">01</span>
          <h3>COMPUTE & INFRASTRUCTURE</h3>
          <p>
            Servers, hosting, storage, networking, development
            infrastructure, domains, testing environments, and the
            boring-but-essential pieces that keep the lab running.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="funding-card">
          <span class="funding-index">02</span>
          <h3>HARDWARE & PROTOTYPING</h3>
          <p>
            Development boards, sensors, embedded systems, electronics,
            fabrication, testing equipment, and experimental hardware.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="funding-card">
          <span class="funding-index">03</span>
          <h3>SOFTWARE & RESEARCH</h3>
          <p>
            Development tools, AI infrastructure, research systems,
            open-source software, documentation, testing, and
            engineering work.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="funding-card">
          <span class="funding-index">04</span>
          <h3>COMMUNITY & ACCESS</h3>
          <p>
            Tools, educational resources, accessibility work,
            community infrastructure, and projects that help more
            people participate in technology.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="funding-callout">
        <div class="callout-symbol">+</div>

        <div>
          <strong>
            WE DON'T WANT SUPPORT TO DISAPPEAR INTO A BLACK BOX.
          </strong>

          <p>
            Barkly is being built around documentation and transparency.
            As the lab grows, we intend to show what we're working on,
            what infrastructure we maintain, and how resources are
            being used.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section ways-section" id="ways">
      <div class="section-number">04 / WAYS TO HELP</div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>
          YOU DON'T HAVE<br />
          <span>TO BE A COMPANY.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          Barkly is being built for people. That means people can help
          build it too.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="support-options">
        <article class="support-card featured">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span>01</span>
            <span>INDIVIDUAL</span>
          </div>

          <h3>SUPPORT THE LAB</h3>

          <p>
            A contribution of any size helps keep the lab moving.
            Small contributions matter because infrastructure is built
            one piece at a time.
          </p>

          <div class="card-bottom">
            <span>PEOPLE →</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="support-card">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span>02</span>
            <span>SPONSOR</span>
          </div>

          <h3>BACK THE WORK</h3>

          <p>
            Organizations can support Barkly through sponsorship,
            project funding, equipment support, infrastructure, or
            other forms of partnership.
          </p>

          <div class="card-bottom">
            <a href="#sponsors">SPONSORS →</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="support-card">
          <div class="card-top">
            <span>03</span>
            <span>NON-MONETARY</span>
          </div>

          <h3>GIVE SOMETHING ELSE</h3>

          <p>
            Hardware, expertise, collaboration, testing, documentation,
            introductions, and thoughtful feedback can all help move a
            project forward.
          </p>

          <div class="card-bottom">
            <span>BUILD WITH US →</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="support-card">
            <div class="card-top">
                <span>04</span>
                <span>SPREAD THE WORD</span>
            </div>

            <h3>HELP PEOPLE FIND BARKLY</h3>

            <p>
                Share Barkly, talk about the projects, connect us with people who
                might care, and help more humans discover what we're building.
            </p>

            <div class="card-bottom">
                <span>SHARE THE LAB →</span>
            </div>
            </article>
      </div>

      <div class="support-message">
        <span class="message-paw">◈</span>

        <div>
          <h3>
            EVEN $5 IS PART OF THE LAB.
          </h3>

          <p>
            Barkly isn't being built by pretending that only giant
            checks matter. A community is made from people deciding
            that something is worth building.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

           <div class="financial-system-banner">
        <div class="financial-system-header">
          <div>
            <span class="financial-system-label">
              FINANCIAL TRANSPARENCY / SYSTEM 001
            </span>

            <h3>
              THE FINANCIAL<br />
              <span>SYSTEM IS BEING BUILT.</span>
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="financial-system-status">
            <span class="financial-status-dot"></span>
            SYSTEM STATUS: IN DEVELOPMENT
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="financial-system-copy">
          <p>
            Barkly Labs is building its own financial transparency
            infrastructure so that support can be tracked, understood,
            reconciled, and reported in a way that makes sense to actual
            humans.
          </p>

          <p>
            The goal isn't to put a pretty number on a page.
            <strong>We want to build the system behind the number.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="financial-system-grid">
          <div class="financial-system-item">
            <span>01</span>

            <div>
              <strong>STATEMENT PARSER</strong>
              <p>
                Import financial records and turn them into structured
                transaction data.
              </p>
            </div>

            <b>BUILDING</b>
          </div>

          <div class="financial-system-item">
            <span>02</span>

            <div>
              <strong>TRANSACTION LEDGER</strong>
              <p>
                Organize income, expenses, transfers, donations, and
                other financial activity.
              </p>
            </div>

            <b>BUILDING</b>
          </div>

          <div class="financial-system-item">
            <span>03</span>

            <div>
              <strong>RECONCILIATION</strong>
              <p>
                Compare imported records and identify transactions
                that require review.
              </p>
            </div>

            <b>NEXT</b>
          </div>

          <div class="financial-system-item">
            <span>04</span>

            <div>
              <strong>PUBLIC REPORTING</strong>
              <p>
                Turn the underlying financial data into a readable
                public financial report.
              </p>
            </div>

            <b>NEXT</b>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="financial-system-principle">
          <div class="financial-principle-mark">+</div>

          <div>
            <span>THE BARKLY PRINCIPLE</span>

            <strong>
              BUILD THE INFRASTRUCTURE.<br />
              THEN SHOW THE NUMBERS.
            </strong>

            <p>
              Barkly would rather build a transparent system properly
              than publish financial information that cannot be verified
              or understood.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="donation-panel">
        <div class="donation-panel-header">
          <span>DONATIONS / 001</span>
          <span>PAYPAL</span>
        </div>

        <div class="donation-panel-content">
          <div>
            <h3>
              HELP KEEP<br />
              <span>BARKLY BUILDING.</span>
            </h3>

            <p>
              Contributions help provide the infrastructure, hardware,
              software, research capacity, and development time needed
              to keep the laboratory moving.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="paypal-container">
            <span>SUPPORT BARKLY LABS</span>

            <strong>DONATE WITH PAYPAL</strong>

            <!-- PayPal Donate Button -->
            <div id="paypal-donate-button-container"></div>

            <small>
              Financial transparency infrastructure is currently
              under development. Public reporting will expand as
              the system comes online.
            </small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section sponsor-section" id="sponsors">
      <div class="section-number">05 / SPONSORSHIP</div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>
          BUILD WITH<br />
          <span>THE LAB.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          Barkly Labs is open to organizations that want to support
          human-centered technology, experimental engineering,
          open infrastructure, and the people building it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sponsor-grid">
        <article class="sponsor-card">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>LAB SPONSORSHIP</h3>
          <p>
            Support the broader laboratory and help maintain the
            infrastructure that allows multiple projects to exist
            and evolve.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="sponsor-card">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>PROJECT SUPPORT</h3>
          <p>
            Support a specific area of development such as AI,
            hardware, documentation, accessibility, plant technology,
            or experimental computing.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="sponsor-card">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>EQUIPMENT & INFRASTRUCTURE</h3>
          <p>
            Help put physical tools and computing infrastructure into
            the lab so ideas can move from software diagrams into
            working systems.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="sponsor-callout">
        <div>
          <span class="callout-label">SPONSORSHIP PRINCIPLE</span>

          <h3>
            PARTNERSHIP SHOULD<br />
            <span>HELP THE WORK.</span>
          </h3>

          <p>
            Barkly will not pretend that a logo on a website is the
            same thing as building something useful. Sponsorship should
            create meaningful capacity for the laboratory and the work
            it exists to do.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a class="primary-button" href="#contact">
          TALK TO THE LAB →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section transparency-section" id="transparency">
      <div class="section-number">06 / TRANSPARENCY</div>

      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>
          SHOW THE<br />
          <span>WORK.</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          Barkly follows a simple principle:
          if we're asking people to believe in the work, we should
          show them the work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="transparency-grid">
        <div class="transparency-item">
          <span>01</span>
          <strong>PUBLIC PROJECTS</strong>
          <p>
            Whenever practical, projects, documentation, requirements,
            and technical work are made visible.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="transparency-item">
          <span>02</span>
          <strong>DOCUMENTED DECISIONS</strong>
          <p>
            Requirements, design choices, experiments, and lessons
            learned should become part of the record.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="transparency-item">
          <span>03</span>
          <strong>NO MAGIC</strong>
          <p>
            Barkly should be understandable enough that another human
            can inspect the system and see how it works.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="transparency-item">
          <span>04</span>
          <strong>HUMAN FIRST</strong>
          <p>
            Transparency isn't only about money. It's also about
            making technology understandable to the people using it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="final-statement">
        <div class="statement-line"></div>

        <p>
          PEOPLE ARE WORTH<br />
          <span>DESIGNING FOR.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="statement-line"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="contact-section" id="contact">
      <div class="contact-inner">
        <div class="section-number">CONTACT / 001</div>

        <h2>
          WANT TO<br />
          <span>BUILD WITH US?</span>
        </h2>

        <p>
          Whether you're an individual, organization, engineer,
          artist, researcher, builder, or simply someone who thinks
          this should exist — there's room in the lab.
        </p>

        <a class="primary-button large-button" href="/contact">
          CONTACT BARKLY →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div>
      <strong>BARKLY LABS</strong>
      <span>HUMAN FIRST</span>
    </div>

    <div>
      SUPPORT / DOCUMENT 001
    </div>
  </footer>
</body>

<style>

    .financial-system-banner {
  margin-top: 50px;
  padding: 45px;
  border: 1px solid #333;
  background:
    linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.09),
      transparent 48%
    ),
    #080808;
}

.financial-system-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 40px;
  padding-bottom: 40px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #292929;
}

.financial-system-label {
  display: block;
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
}

.financial-system-header h3 {
  margin: 25px 0 0;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(38px, 5vw, 72px);
  line-height: 0.9;
  letter-spacing: -0.065em;
}

.financial-system-header h3 span {
  color: #ff2f92;
}

.financial-system-status {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
  padding: 10px 13px;
  border: 1px solid #333;
  color: #a1a1a1;
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

.financial-status-dot {
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: #ff2f92;
  box-shadow: 0 0 12px rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.7);
}

.financial-system-copy {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 50px;
  padding: 38px 0;
}

.financial-system-copy p {
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 0;
  color: #a1a1a1;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.financial-system-copy strong {
  color: #f1f1f1;
}

.financial-system-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 1px;
  background: #292929;
  border: 1px solid #292929;
}

.financial-system-item {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 35px 1fr auto;
  gap: 20px;
  align-items: start;
  min-height: 185px;
  padding: 28px;
  background: #050505;
}

.financial-system-item > span {
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 10px;
}

.financial-system-item strong {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}

.financial-system-item p {
  max-width: 430px;
  margin: 0;
  color: #686868;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.financial-system-item b {
  padding: 5px 8px;
  border: 1px solid #333;
  color: #686868;
  font-size: 8px;
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
}

.financial-system-item:nth-child(-n + 2) b {
  border-color: rgba(255, 47, 146, 0.4);
  color: #ff2f92;
}

.financial-system-principle {
  display: flex;
  gap: 25px;
  margin-top: 35px;
  padding: 30px;
  border-left: 2px solid #ff2f92;
  background: #0c0c0c;
}

.financial-principle-mark {
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 30px;
}

.financial-system-principle > div > span {
  display: block;
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.financial-system-principle strong {
  display: block;
  margin: 18px 0;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 38px);
  line-height: 0.95;
  letter-spacing: -0.04em;
}

.financial-system-principle p {
  max-width: 700px;
  margin: 0;
  color: #a1a1a1;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.55;
}

.donation-panel {
  margin-top: 35px;
  padding: 35px;
  border: 1px solid #333;
  background: #080808;
}

.donation-panel-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  padding-bottom: 18px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #292929;
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.donation-panel-content {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.7fr;
  gap: 70px;
  align-items: center;
  padding-top: 35px;
}

.donation-panel-content h3 {
  margin: 0 0 20px;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: clamp(34px, 4vw, 58px);
  line-height: 0.9;
  letter-spacing: -0.055em;
}

.donation-panel-content h3 span {
  color: #ff2f92;
}

.donation-panel-content > div:first-child p {
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 0;
  color: #a1a1a1;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1.55;
}

.paypal-container {
  padding: 30px;
  border: 1px solid #333;
  text-align: center;
  background: #050505;
}

.paypal-container > span {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 15px;
  color: #ff2f92;
  font-size: 9px;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
}

.paypal-container strong {
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 25px;
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  font-size: 21px;
}

.paypal-container small {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 20px;
  color: #686868;
  font-size: 9px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

@media (max-width: 800px) {
  .financial-system-banner {
    padding: 28px;
  }

  .financial-system-header {
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .financial-system-copy,
  .financial-system-grid,
  .donation-panel-content {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .financial-system-item {
    min-height: auto;
  }

  .donation-panel-content {
    gap: 40px;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .financial-system-banner,
  .donation-panel {
    padding: 22px;
  }

  .financial-system-item {
    grid-template-columns: 25px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .financial-system-item b {
    grid-column: 2;
    justify-self: start;
  }

  .financial-system-principle {
    padding: 24px;
  }

  .paypal-container {
    padding: 25px;
  }
}

  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #050505;
    color: #f1f1f1;
    font-family:
      "Courier New",
      Courier,
